4023 * gabba 'filling of a hole'. 2. * gampa-. 1. N. gāb , gāp 'rubble for filling in a wall, strong
foundation stone of a wall'; G. gābṛī f. 'filling of a hole';
M. gābḍẽ n. 'patch for a hole'. 2. S. gamba f. 'mud building' ( g !). * gabhara- 'deep' see gabhīrá -. * gabhīna- 'deep' see next.
